  actor: jgstern_agent  # ce45
  clock: 5  # ce45
  nonce: ce45  # ce45
  message: "Status on the inert pool:\n\n**Plan exists**, no implementation yet. **WI-gudob** (P3 todo_soft, created 2026-04-18T02:21Z — 19 min after this registry landed) is the umbrella tracker item for tackling it. Per INV-nimuj, it prioritizes by producer count, which is a direct proxy for false-positive-reduction volume. Top candidates from the current scan:\n\n| Concept | Producers | Candidate linker shape |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error_handler | 37 | Protocol — HTTP error-response registration |\n| controller | 34 | Framework — route-group containment |\n| websocket_handler | 21 | Protocol — ws dispatch |\n| event_handler | 17 | Protocol — may overlap with message_dispatch.py |\n| application | 17 | Infrastructure — app-root containment |\n\n**Why no code yet:** WI-gudob is P3; the P2 rust-analyzer SCIP backend chain (WI-bajuz → WI-mafut → WI-duzul) has been consuming the attention budget. WI-bajuz just closed (commit ccf60c39f); WI-mafut is next in P2. No linker PR has landed for any inert concept since this registry was created — the pool is still 310/316, unchanged from the first scan.\n\n**Open question for you:** should WI-gudob be bumped to P2, putting it ahead of the rust-analyzer package scaffold? The trade-off:\n- Bumping it means 1 Protocol linker on the next PR (error_handler or controller → ~30+ frameworks' dispatch edges recovered)\n- Leaving it P3 means the SCIP backend lands first, which unblocks WI-duzul + WI-nokoh (rust-analyzer-package scaffold + descriptor decoder) — a bigger but longer-payoff move\n\nNo status change pending until you weigh in."  # ce45
